+# Light Tool Secure V2 — INPROGRESS
+
+55 canonical source registrations were generated and proxy-read back with the
+selected SDK. This corrects the historical 43-converted/12-missing-SDK labels;
+those old labels do not describe current source. No whole-pack pass follows.
+
+All 55 purpose rows are retained in validation/PURPOSE_MATRIX.json. That review
+found no demonstrated missing SDK function or blanket node refusal for the
+inspected purposes. Exact final dependency/profile/runtime/Guest and original
+behavior qualification remains pending. Historical six typed-node 26-case
+native/ordinary-Guest evidence applies only to its original source tuple.
+
+Public ImageRef.from_tensor and MaskRef.from_value preserve native IMAGE/MASK
+rank and kind. URL nodes use genuine managed assets.fetch_bytes/import_url
+(HTTP and HTTPS default ports80/443), copy_input and owned-import lifecycle.
+LoadImageFromURL requests raw/assets/assets.import_url; metadata requests
+assets/assets.import_url/assets.import_url.manage, without broad assets.delete.
+Real signed Light pack admission and authenticated provider consent remain
+required. Explicit isolated authority fixtures do not provide that grant.
+
+URL qualification still includes native codecs/status/error/body/filename and
+same-basename concurrency parity, cancellation/ref/OOB/lease/death cleanup,
+private-IP/DNS/redirect/host/capability enforcement and real Guest delivery.
+The isolated provider component now has separate current native-nine and
+required-Seatbelt Guest-nine passes. One real Mac Guest fetched the exact8090B
+HTTP PNG and enforced private-IP/DNS, public80-to443-to-private redirect,
+capability and host refusals with no private connection. Actual argv/profile,
+supported runtime roots, constructor/module origins and independent cleanup
+were recorded; source/runtime/site maps were unchanged. This is a public-SDK
+probe under isolated fixture authority, not an admitted Light-node or signed
+service pass. Earlier harness failures remain preserved. See the20261019 HTTP
+Guest evidence addendum and strict receipt c91c940145109a9c824001502f305fa17d4c83334d8570f355e4a58a98d9b76c.
+Full64MiB fetch and large IPC support remain unqualified. Existing user HTTP
+authorization does not grant arbitrary sockets or Aliyun access.
+
+Video preview/load/save require actual admitted managed-media descriptors,
+exact-byte copy, selected codecs, owned media lifetime and frontend/provider
+integration. Aliyun upload additionally requires integrations.aliyun_oss and
+separate real account policy/credentials; HTTP authorization does not grant it.
+OpenCV/image nodes require a compatible locked scientific/native closure.
+pyproject lists numpy/pillow/torch/opencv-python-headless/httpx but exact target
+pins/ABI closure and immutable profile must be supplied externally.
+
+SaveAsJPG has scoped earlier evidence on a separate grayscale-JPEG SDK delta.
+Exact directory-name listing and managed UTF8 caption overwrite/error-order
+parity require the separately proposed confined JPEG API contribution and its
+qualification. That contribution is not silently folded into the canonical
+f1a73e4f SDK pin. Final JPEG source/runtime support is not certified here.
+
+Canonical secure-nodes.json now contains the actual55generated declarations,
+including six URL permission declarations and metadata managed-import rights.
+It is not a provider/service grant. Current admission/installed-runtime/browser
+acceptance remains pending. Refer to SDK_REQUIREMENTS.json and top-level README.
+
